mutation finish a backend failure without producing a response
detects TypeOK
only one configured
-                     ![r].response = requests[r].result]
+                     ![r].response = IF requests[r].result = "failed" THEN "none" ELSE requests[r].result]

mutation issue a cookie on an unrecognized POST code
detects CookieRequiresMatchingPost
only one configured
-    /\ LET approvedCode == Configured /\ requests[r].credential = "match"
+    /\ LET approvedCode == Configured /\ requests[r].credential \in {"match", "other"}

mutation issue a cookie when the configured digest is missing
detects CookieRequiresMatchingPost
only blank digest
-    /\ LET approvedCode == Configured /\ requests[r].credential = "match"
+    /\ LET approvedCode == requests[r].credential = "match"

mutation issue a cookie from a form that failed the request transport checks
detects CookieRequiresMatchingPost
only one configured
-                         ![r].response = CASE ~requests[r].validInput -> "blocked"
+                         ![r].response = CASE FALSE -> "blocked"

mutation use the POST code path to initiate a private query
detects QueryRequiresRootGet
only one configured
-                        [] route = "postRoot" -> "codeCheck"
+                        [] route = "postRoot" -> "cookieCheck"

mutation let a non-root request query the audit backend
detects QueryRequiresRootGet
only one configured
-                        [] OTHER -> "done",
+                        [] route = "wrongPath" -> "cookieCheck"
+                        [] OTHER -> "done",

mutation trust a query or header claim instead of the verified cookie
detects QueryRequiresMatchingCookie
only one configured
-    /\ LET approvedCookie == Configured /\ requests[r].credential = "match"
+    /\ LET approvedCookie == Configured /\ (requests[r].credential = "match" \/ requests[r].claim)

mutation start the private query when the cookie verifier errors
detects QueryRequiresMatchingCookie
only one configured
-    /\ LET approvedCookie == Configured /\ requests[r].credential = "match"
+    /\ LET approvedCookie == Configured /\ requests[r].credential \in {"match", "error"}

mutation permit a cookie although the configured digest is missing
detects QueryRequiresMatchingCookie
only blank digest
-    /\ LET approvedCookie == Configured /\ requests[r].credential = "match"
+    /\ LET approvedCookie == requests[r].credential = "match"

mutation reuse a previous request's valid-cookie decision for another request
detects QueryRequiresMatchingCookie
only two concurrent
-    /\ LET approvedCookie == Configured /\ requests[r].credential = "match"
+    /\ LET approvedCookie == Configured /\ (requests[r].credential = "match" \/
+                   (\E peer \in RequestIds \ {r} : requests[peer].phase \in {"approved", "query"}))

mutation send invalid dates or pages to the audit object
detects QueryRequiresValidInput
only one configured
-    /\ LET mayQuery == requests[r].validInput
+    /\ LET mayQuery == TRUE

mutation use another request's ready rows when the current backend query fails
detects RowsStayWithRequest
only two concurrent
-     /\ requests' = [requests EXCEPT ![r].result = result,
-          ![r].origin = IF result = "rows" THEN r ELSE 0,
-          ![r].phase = "render"]
+     /\ LET donors == {peer \in RequestIds \ {r} : requests[peer].result = "rows"}
+            borrowed == IF result = "failed" /\ donors # {} THEN (CHOOSE peer \in donors : TRUE) ELSE 0
+        IN requests' = [requests EXCEPT ![r].result = IF borrowed # 0 THEN "rows" ELSE result,
+             ![r].origin = IF borrowed # 0 THEN borrowed ELSE IF result = "rows" THEN r ELSE 0,
+             ![r].phase = "render"]
